================================================================================
Modifications (Apache-2.0 §4(b))
================================================================================

  * Renamed the CLI command (and log prefix) from "ocr" to "codecheck" to avoid
    colliding with "optical character recognition". The upstream OpenCodeReview
    brand and attribution are preserved.
  * Hard-wired three fixed review rules ahead of LoadDefault, so they apply with
    zero configuration: security & desensitization, bug finding, and redundant /
    out-of-scope code.
  * Windows: subprocesses are spawned hidden (no console windows).
  * Cross-platform process-tree termination, so a cancelled review leaves no
    orphaned child processes.
  * Removed the ChatGPT account (OAuth) authentication channel
    (upstream internal/chatgptauth/, cmd/opencodereview/chatgpt_auth.go,
    internal/llm/chatgpt.go).
  * Kept upstream's sensitive-path exclusion: files matching sensitive patterns
    (.ssh, private keys, .env, ...) are never sent to the model.

The modified source lives in engine/. Every source file keeps its upstream
`SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` line and copyright header.

